 "result": "All of it is in `src/tessel/views.py`, plus one read of `view_func.methods` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py`.\n\n1. **Class setup:** `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (`views.py:165`) runs when you subclass. It collects the HTTP verbs the class defines (`get`, `post`, …) from `http_method_funcs`, upper-cases them, merges in any base-class `methods`, and sets `cls.methods`.\n\n2. **Class → view function:** `View.to_view_func(name, ...)` (`views.py:86`) is a classmethod that builds a closure `view(**kwargs)`:\n   - By default it creates a new instance per request, `view.view_class(*class_args, **class_kwargs)`, and calls `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`.\n   - If `init_every_request` is `False`, it shares one instance.\n   - It applies `cls.decorators`.\n   - It copies `view_class`, `__name__`, `__doc__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function (`:129-134`).\n\n3. **Route registration:** `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`) reads `view_func.methods` (`:623`, defaulting to `(\"GET\",)`). That makes the URL rule accept exactly the verbs the class defines.\n\n4. **Per-request dispatch:** `VerbView.run_view` (`views.py:182`) does `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`, falls back to `get` for `HEAD` when there is no `head` handler, asserts a handler exists, and calls it through `ensure_sync` with the URL kwargs.\n\nThe base `View.run_view` (`views.py:78`) is what you override for a non-verb-dispatched view.",
